Repair the complete CommonJS source below. Export exactly `{ isPowerOfTen }` in the corrected source.

`isPowerOfTen(value)` must return `true` only for positive safe integers equal to an integer power of ten, including `1` as 10⁰. It returns `false` for zero, negative numbers, non-integers, unsafe integers, infinities, `NaN`, and non-number values. It must not coerce inputs or mutate anything.

```javascript
function isPowerOfTen(value) {
  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(value) || value === 0) return false;
  return Number.isInteger(Math.log10(Math.abs(value)));
}

module.exports = { isPowerOfTen };
```

